    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "AmericanAirlines\nWORLDWIDE\nTimetable\nPassenger Schedule and Cargo Guide. Includes American Eagle.\nEFFECTIVE JUNE 15, 1992\nAMERICAN AIRLINES\nIS BRINGING VALUE\nBACK TO AIR TRAVEL.",
      "GET\nMORE\nMILEAGE\nOUT OF\nYOUR\nCREDIT CARD.\nCITIBANK+\n\"Advantage®\nAmericanAirlines®\n4128\n4128 123\n45b\nVALID FROM\nEXPIRATION DATE\n02/92\n01/31/93\nCV\nC STEPHENS\nWENREE 92\n789\nVISA®\nThe Citibank A\"Advantage card\nearns you free worldwide travel on\nAmerican Airlines.\nA\nEvery time you use the Citibank AAdvantage MasterCard® or Visa® to make\na purchase, you'll earn one Advantage mile for every dollar you spend\n• It's the quickest way to earn free travel on American Airlines\nYou can redeem your Advantage miles for travel awards to exciting destinations in the\nUnited States, Europe, the Orient, Australia, South America, and the Caribbean.\nSo apply today for the Citibank AAdvantage card. The annual fee is $50.* No other card gives\nyou more ways to earn free travel on American Airlines.\nPick up an application at any American Airlines airport location or city ticket office.\nTO APPLY BY PHONE, CALL 1-800-FLY-4444, EXT. 60.\nAmerican Airlines and AAdvantage are registered trademarks of American Airlines, Inc. American Airlines reserves the right to change the Advantage program at any\ntime without notice. The Citibank Advantage card is issued by Citibank (South Dakota), N.A.\n*The anual percentage rate for purchases and advances is 19.8%. If a finance charge is imposed, the minimum is $50. There is an additional transaction fee finance\ncharge of $1.75 for each cash advance obtained at an Automated Teller Machine (ATM). If the cash advance is obtained via check, or at a financial institution\n(without using an ATM), the additional finance charge will equal 2% of the amount of each cash advance; however, it will not be less than $2.00 or more than$ 10.00\n© 1992 Citibank (South Dakota), N.A. Member F.D.I.C"
    ],
